            "basis": "The same article's alternative reading of the same peg: \"following Eusebius (Church History III.5.2), it is possible to fix the definitive departure of the Apostles about the year 60, in which event the writing of the Gospel would have taken place about the year 60-68.\" The article presents this beside the 40-42 reckoning without choosing between them.",
            "basis_class": "traditional-catholic",
            "date": "60 A.D. to 68 A.D.",
            "derived": false,
            "disposition": "disputed",
            "inherited": true,
            "label": "about the year 60-68",
            "note": "",
            "precision": "interval",
            "profile": "catholic-traditional-v1",
            "relation": "composition",
            "reporting_exception": null,
            "scope": "Matt",
            "sources": [
              "artifact.catholic-encyclopedia.volume-10.new-york-1911.newadvent-10057a-e7b6ccef"
            ],
            "subject": "composition.gospel-of-matthew",
            "title": "The Gospel of St Matthew"
          },
          {
            "answerability": "answerable",
            "basis": "The same article quotes St Irenaeus, \"somewhat more exact concerning the date of the First Gospel\": \"Matthew produced his Gospel when Peter and Paul were evangelizing and founding the Church of Rome, consequently about the years 64-67.\"",
            "basis_class": "reported-traditional",
            "date": "64 A.D. to 67 A.D.",
            "derived": false,
            "disposition": "disputed",
            "inherited": true,
            "label": "about the years 64-67",
            "note": "The article at once qualifies the testimony: \"However, this text presents difficulties of interpretation which render its meaning uncertain and prevent us from deducing any positive conclusion.\"",
            "precision": "interval",
            "profile": "catholic-traditional-v1",
            "relation": "composition",
            "reporting_exception": null,
            "scope": "Matt",
            "sources": [
              "artifact.catholic-encyclopedia.volume-10.new-york-1911.newadvent-10057a-e7b6ccef"
            ],
            "subject": "composition.gospel-of-matthew",
            "title": "The Gospel of St Matthew"
          },
          {
            "answerability": "answerable",
            "basis": "Durand's article \"The New Testament\" in the Catholic Encyclopedia (vol. 14, 1912) dates the lost Aramaic Matthew instead: \"The original text of St. Matthew is certainly prior to the ruin of Jerusalem, there are even reasons for dating it earlier than the Epistles of St. Paul and consequently about the year 50.\"",
            "basis_class": "traditional-catholic",
            "date": "about 50 A.D.",
            "derived": false,
            "disposition": "disputed",
            "inherited": true,
            "label": "about the year 50",
            "note": "This dates the Aramaic original, not the canonical Greek text: the next sentence says \"We know nothing definite of the date of its being rendered into Greek.\" A consumer that reads it as the date of the Greek Matthew is reading it wrongly.",
            "precision": "approximate-year",
            "profile": "catholic-traditional-v1",
            "relation": "composition",
            "reporting_exception": null,
            "scope": "Matt",
            "sources": [
              "artifact.catholic-encyclopedia.volume-14.new-york-1912.newadvent-14530a-0a19aa2c"
            ],
            "subject": "composition.gospel-of-matthew",
            "title": "The Gospel of St Matthew"
          }
        ],
        "chronology_status": "composition-only",
        "locus": "Matt.20.15",
        "reason": "",
        "requested_profile": "catholic-comprehensive-v1",
        "resolved_profiles": {
          "composition": "catholic-traditional-v1"
        },
        "status": "ok",
        "v": 1
      }
